{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And behold, an olive leaf plucked in her mouth.</b> From the expression ״כל טרפי צמחה״ — which is explained as a cluster of blossoms (סמדר). Therefore Noah knew that the waters had abated, for if not so, but he inferred it from the dove's having found something large — how would he know? For perhaps she found it floating on the water. Rather, because he saw it was a blossom-cluster, he knew she had taken it from a tree."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:11.951584942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}